    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1606">

                <pb facs="1312" n="1196" xml:id="pg1196"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.77/92.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 12.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-12-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 12, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 15 of
                    the 29th ultimo, reporting the conversation between yourself and Mr. Augusto
                    Dziuk, the representative of the Balboa and Pacific Estates Company Limited and
                    the Balboa and Darien Estates and Railway Company, in regard to the railroad
                    concession granted to these companies.</p>
                <p>Copies of your despatch and the English text of the enclosure have been forwarded
                    to the Secretary of War.</p>
                <p>The Department’s views as to this concession are covered by instruction No. 89,
                    of September 20, 1911, to Mr. Andrews.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
